    "https://www.colum.edu/careers-and-alumni/industry-opportunities": {
      "title": "Industry Partnerships",
      "description": "Industry Partnerships | Columbia College Chicago Skip to main content Academics Schools Audio and Music Business and Entrepreneurship Communication and Culture Design Fashion Film and Television Theatre and Dance Visual Arts Programs Majors Minors Graduate Certificate Pre-College Programs Immersive Studies Study Abroad Semester in LA Comedy Studies Academic Resources Academic Advising Academic Calendar Catalog Experential Learning Library Our Faculty Student Tools MyColumbia Portal Canvas Engage IT Assistance Student Hub Admissions + Financial Aid Why Choose Columbia? Chicago: Our City and Campus World-Class Facilities Faculty Mentors and Makers Industry Connections Alumni Success Student Work How to Apply Freshman Transfer Graduate International Second Bachelor's Returning Students Nondegree Seeking Portfolio and Audition Requirements Cost + Aid Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition and Fees Admitted Students Undergraduate Graduate Orientation Visit Us Campus Visits Virtual Tours Student Experience Campus Life Student Center Student Organizations Athletics and Recreation Student Spotlights Events on Campus Manifest Arts Festival Housing + Living Campus Housing Options Office of Housing and Residential Experience Living in Chicago Campus Facilities Campus Map Services + Support Campus Safety and Security Student Health Support Services MyColumbia Portal Information Technology Student Handbook Student Success Student Financial Services Academic Advising Belonging and Persistence Holistic Support Career Outcomes Career Advising Alumni Success Rankings and Awards About About the College Facts Mission and History Rankings and Awards Academic Access and Excellence Strategic Plan Contact Us Leadership Office of the President Office of the Provost Board of Trustees News + Events Columbia Stories Media Mentions Event Spotlight 135th Anniversary Media Resources Careers + Alumni Career Center Internships Job Board Industry Partnerships Alumni Success The Alumni Network Get Info Apply Visit Give Search colum.edu Quick Links MyColumbia Canvas Library Academic Calendar Commencement Campus Map Building Hours Resources For Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Student Counselors and Advocates Faculty and Staff Alumni Donors Employers Health + Safety Campus Safety and Security Health Services Center for Student Wellbeing Services for Students with Disabilities Report a Concern Get Connected Give to Columbia Work at Columbia Hire from Columbia Directory Contact Us Get Info Apply Visit Give Search and quick links Open navigation menu Ready to Work with Industry Leaders? Imagine turning classroom theory into real-world experience with top companies like L’Oréal, NASCAR, and Hilton Hotels and Resorts. Columbia College Chicago doesn’t just teach creative disciplines; we connect you to the industries that use them. Working with our vast network of industry partners can help you get a head start on your career, including: Real-world experience Columbia College Chicago gives you access to the creative world you’re passionate about. Forget textbook scenarios—you’ll gain practical experience by collaborating with industry professionals on real-world projects. These collaborations allow you to apply your skills in a tangible way and offer valuable industry exposure through internships and project partnerships. Portfolio power Your projects and experiences at Columbia will feed directly into your portfolio. You’ll create a collection of work that showcases your talent, technical skills, and problem-solving abilities—all directly relevant to your desired industry. This will become your calling card, setting you apart from the competition when you apply for jobs or freelance opportunities. Network advantage At Columbia, you’ll be surrounded by inspiring peers, dedicated faculty, and industry professionals. These connections create a powerful network that can open doors to future opportunities. You’ll build lasting relationships with classmates, mentors, and industry partners that can lead to job recommendations, collaborations, and a supportive network as you launch your career. OUR INDUSTRY PARTNERS Concept to Consumer Columbia students partnered with YKK, Browzwear, and SOUNDOFF to design inclusive bridalwear and custom Chicago Sky fan apparel—real-world projects powered by industry collaboration. Students Bring Gift Bag Designs to Market Students at Columbia College Chicago learn the art and business of design thanks to partnership with gift bag seller Dipak and marketing firm Madak . Agency: Students Deliver Real-World Marketing Campaigns In this Columbia-produced video, students in Kevin Christophersen’s “Agency” class discuss the marketing strategies, ads, social media plans, and other deliverables they developed to created integrated campaigns for real-world startup clients. Columbia College Chicago Students Experience the Ultimate Field Trip Business and Entrepreneurship students take their education beyond the classroom each year at SXSW , gaining practical experience working with real clients. From Classroom to Industry: Students Lead at Unleashed 2023 Columbia bridges the classroom and career by partnering with industry leaders, like those behind Unleashed 2023’s activations, where Business and Entrepreneurship students received course credit for their hands-on planning and design work. Columbia Students Partner With Patagonia for Worn Wear Competition Patagonia partnered with Columbia students to showcase innovative designs, all crafted from recycled Patagonia materials. The project highlighted the intersection of fashion and environmental responsibility. Columbia Team Wins U.S. L’Oréal Brandstorm Competition for Fourth Year in a Row Columbia College Chicago were named the U.S. winners of L’Oréal Brandstorm, an annual international student competition that gives students the chance to tackle a real business case, gain new skills, and engage with industry experts. Columbia Students Partner With NASCAR Chicago to Create Race-Themed Games NASCAR Chicago Street Race partnered with Columbia students to create family-friendly interactive digital activities and a print publication for the Chicago street race. Illustration Student Creates Sweet Design for Fannie May Fannie May Chocolates unveiled the newest iteration of their Chicago Line. The packaging is designed by Illustration alum Katelyn McManis ‘22 and features the city’s most iconic landmarks. McManis was connected to this early career opportunity through The Career Center. Read More Visit Career Center Columbia College Chicago homepage Columbia College Chicago Instagram Columbia College Chicago Facebook Columbia College Chicago LinkedIn Columbia College Chicago YouTube Academics Admissions + Financial Aid Student Experience About Careers & Alumni INFO FOR Students Faculty and Staff Parents Alumni Contact Us Academics Schools Majors & Programs Academic Calendar Our Faculty Request Info Admissions + Financial Aid Application Requirements Portfolios and Auditions Financial Aid Scholarships Apply Student Experience Housing Campus Facilities Support Services Student Success Visit About News Events Rankings and Awards Mission and History Report a Concern Careers & Alumni Alumni Success Career Center Industry Opportunities The Alumni Network Give © 2026 Columbia College Chicago Directory Site Map Privacy Policy Accessibility Consumer Information Accreditation Suggest an Edit × ×"
    },
    "https://www.colum.edu/careers-and-alumni/alumni-success": {
      "title": "Alumni Success",
      "description": "Alumni Success | Columbia College Chicago Skip to main content Academics Schools Audio and Music Business and Entrepreneurship Communication and Culture Design Fashion Film and Television Theatre and Dance Visual Arts Programs Majors Minors Graduate Certificate Pre-College Programs Immersive Studies Study Abroad Semester in LA Comedy Studies Academic Resources Academic Advising Academic Calendar Catalog Experential Learning Library Our Faculty Student Tools MyColumbia Portal Canvas Engage IT Assistance Student Hub Admissions + Financial Aid Why Choose Columbia? Chicago: Our City and Campus World-Class Facilities Faculty Mentors and Makers Industry Connections Alumni Success Student Work How to Apply Freshman Transfer Graduate International Second Bachelor's Returning Students Nondegree Seeking Portfolio and Audition Requirements Cost + Aid Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition and Fees Admitted Students Undergraduate Graduate Orientation Visit Us Campus Visits Virtual Tours Student Experience Campus Life Student Center Student Organizations Athletics and Recreation Student Spotlights Events on Campus Manifest Arts Festival Housing + Living Campus Housing Options Office of Housing and Residential Experience Living in Chicago Campus Facilities Campus Map Services + Support Campus Safety and Security Student Health Support Services MyColumbia Portal Information Technology Student Handbook Student Success Student Financial Services Academic Advising Belonging and Persistence Holistic Support Career Outcomes Career Advising Alumni Success Rankings and Awards About About the College Facts Mission and History Rankings and Awards Academic Access and Excellence Strategic Plan Contact Us Leadership Office of the President Office of the Provost Board of Trustees News + Events Columbia Stories Media Mentions Event Spotlight 135th Anniversary Media Resources Careers + Alumni Career Center Internships Job Board Industry Partnerships Alumni Success The Alumni Network Get Info Apply Visit Give Search colum.edu Quick Links MyColumbia Canvas Library Academic Calendar Commencement Campus Map Building Hours Resources For Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Student Counselors and Advocates Faculty and Staff Alumni Donors Employers Health + Safety Campus Safety and Security Health Services Center for Student Wellbeing Services for Students with Disabilities Report a Concern Get Connected Give to Columbia Work at Columbia Hire from Columbia Directory Contact Us Get Info Apply Visit Give Search and quick links Open navigation menu Pictured above: NBC 5 News Anchor and 2006 Alum Evrod Cassimy Alumni SUCCESS Discover where a degree from Columbia College Chicago can take you. Our alumni are shaping today’s creative industries—working for major networks, launching their own ventures, and earning recognition across the arts, media, and business. Explore how they’re making an impact—and how you can, too. Top Creative Industry Employers Top Alumni Occupations Chief Executives Producers and Directors Marketing Managers Graphic Designers General and Operations Manager Top Cities of Highest Alumni Concentration Chicago Los Angeles New York/New Jersey Detroit Denver 96% of our graduates report being employed* Creative careers start here. Jessica Durbala ’21 animator and 3D modeler Jessica Durbala specializes in motion graphics and animation, as well as CG modeling, live-action filming, and video editing. With three years of experience at American Pinball, she has developed a diverse skill set, from creatively directing a pinball game to filming and designing marketing promos and tutorials. She has filmed a wide range of live-action content, from mechanical tutorials to creative pieces for pinball machines. Read More Paul Garnes ’96 producer and production manager Paul Garnes is an experienced producer, line producer, and production manager with a career spanning major studios like Disney, Dreamworks, HBO, and Paramount Pictures. He has held key roles at Foxx/King Productions and Simmons-Lathan Media Group. Garnes was recruited by Tyler Perry in 2006, where he oversaw operations and production, including the creation of Perry’s studio and backlot. He produced Ava DuVernay’s acclaimed 2011 film Middle of Nowhere and executive produced Selma in 2014, which earned multiple award nominations, including Academy Award and Golden Globe recognition. Garnes also produced the final season of the popular BET series The Game . Read More Michael Goi ’80 director, cinematographer, and writer Michael Goi, ASC, ISC is a highly accomplished director, cinematographer, and writer. He has directed popular television shows such as “Avatar: The Last Airbender,” “The Rookie,” and “The Chilling Adventures of Sabrina,” and wrote and directed the viral film “Megan Is Missing.” With over 70 narrative credits as a cinematographer, Goi’s work includes “American Horror Story,” “Glee,” and “Salem.” He has earned four Emmy nominations and recognition from the American Society of Cinematographers (ASC) for his achievements. A past president of the ASC and an Honorary Member of the Indian Society of Cinematographers, Goi is also an advocate for international collaboration in cinematography. Read More Megan Hammond ’22 Singer-songwriter Chicago-based singer-songwriter Megan Hammond, known professionally as m.e.h., has been making waves in the music scene with her unique blend of neo-soul and pop. After moving to Chicago in 2018 to attend Columbia’s Contemporary, Jazz, and Popular Music program, Hammond quickly gained attention for her standout vocal performances. Her genre-defying sound has earned her recognition, including a recent interview with WBEZ. Now 24, Hammond continues to captivate audiences with her innovative and vulnerable approach to music, performing at events like Lollapalooza’s Chicago Made Music Showcase on her birthday, and solidifying her place in the industry as an emerging artist. Read More Katherine Iorio ’13 journalist and Emmy-winning producer Katherine Iorio is an Emmy Award-winning producer for CNN, an international journalist, and a media consultant from Chicago. She holds a BA in Journalism from Columbia College Chicago and an MA in International Journalism from City University London. Katherine has covered a range of significant events in Chicago, including the NATO Summit and the 2012 Presidential Election, as well as international stories such as the Pope’s Holy Land Tour, the conflict in Ukraine, and the Ebola outbreak in West Africa during her time in London from 2013 to 2014. Read More Jacey Rhorer ’00 Founder of Rhorer Couture Jacey Rhorer founded Rhorer Couture with the understanding that a hat just isn’t a hat—it is a visual reminder of power, beauty, diversity, femininity and expression. Her hat-making journey started during a millinery class at Columbia College Chicago, where she obtained a BA in Fashion Design. Recently, Rhorer’s talents landed her the profound position and coveted title—The Official Milliner of the Kentucky Derby Festival. Helping others exert confidence and self-expression through her designs has fueled Rhorer’s passion and paved the way to accomplishing her dreams. Read More Mac McGuire ’24 Muralist/Illustrator Mac McGuire has worked as a muralist in Chicago since graduating with a bachelor’s degree in Illustration in 2024. She is currently working on her third self-published comic and has several mural proposals in the works. McGuire had the opportunity to come back to Columbia for a commissioned mural honoring the school’s 135 anniversary in 2025. Read More Jonathan McReynolds ’11 Grammy-winning Gospel artist Jonathan McReynolds, a Grammy Award-winning singer, songwriter, and musician from Chicago, has risen to prominence in Christian and contemporary gospel music. With collaborations with artists like Stevie Wonder, H.E.R., and Justin Bieber, McReynolds has earned numerous accolades, including 15 Stellars, 4 Doves, and BMI's Songwriter of the Year and Champion’s Award. He has also achieved six consecutive #1 radio singles and starred in the BET movie Favorite Son and TV series Sunday Best. Read More Joseph Sikora ’98 Film and TV actor Joseph Sikora is an award-winning American actor who studied acting at the Piven Theatre Workshop in Evanston, Illinois, and at Columbia College Chicago where he received his BA degree in Theatre. Since 2014, Sikora has starred as “Tommy Egan” in the Power series (Power, Power Book II: Ghost, Power Book IV: Force). He also acted in Ozark, Chicago PD, and the animated series, Teenage Euthanasia. Read More Asha Ward ’21 Stand-up comedian featured on Netflix and Comedy Central Asha Ward is a stand-up comedian, actor and writer based in NYC. She graduated from Columbia College Chicago in 2021 with a BA in Comedic Writing and Performance. She currently writes for Saturday Night Live and joined the 48th season as the show's youngest ever writer. She received her first Emmy nomination in 2023 for Outstanding Writing for a Variety Series. Her stand up has been featured on Netflix and Comedy Central. Read More Industry Opportunities Alumni stories Career Center * Rates are based on institutional surveys – Learn More Columbia College Chicago homepage Columbia College Chicago Instagram Columbia College Chicago Facebook Columbia College Chicago LinkedIn Columbia College Chicago YouTube Academics Admissions + Financial Aid Student Experience About Careers & Alumni INFO FOR Students Faculty and Staff Parents Alumni Contact Us Academics Schools Majors & Programs Academic Calendar Our Faculty Request Info Admissions + Financial Aid Application Requirements Portfolios and Auditions Financial Aid Scholarships Apply Student Experience Housing Campus Facilities Support Services Student Success Visit About News Events Rankings and Awards Mission and History Report a Concern Careers & Alumni Alumni Success Career Center Industry Opportunities The Alumni Network Give © 2026 Columbia College Chicago Directory Site Map Privacy Policy Accessibility Consumer Information Accreditation Suggest an Edit × ×"
    },
    "https://www.colum.edu/careers-and-alumni/career-center/students/appointments": {
      "title": "Career Center",
      "description": "Career Center | Columbia College Chicago Skip to main content Academics Schools Audio and Music Business and Entrepreneurship Communication and Culture Design Fashion Film and Television Theatre and Dance Visual Arts Programs Majors Minors Graduate Certificate Pre-College Programs Immersive Studies Study Abroad Semester in LA Comedy Studies Academic Resources Academic Advising Academic Calendar Catalog Experential Learning Library Our Faculty Student Tools MyColumbia Portal Canvas Engage IT Assistance Student Hub Admissions + Financial Aid Why Choose Columbia? Chicago: Our City and Campus World-Class Facilities Faculty Mentors and Makers Industry Connections Alumni Success Student Work How to Apply Freshman Transfer Graduate International Second Bachelor's Returning Students Nondegree Seeking Portfolio and Audition Requirements Cost + Aid Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition and Fees Admitted Students Undergraduate Graduate Orientation Visit Us Campus Visits Virtual Tours Student Experience Campus Life Student Center Student Organizations Athletics and Recreation Student Spotlights Events on Campus Manifest Arts Festival Housing + Living Campus Housing Options Office of Housing and Residential Experience Living in Chicago Campus Facilities Campus Map Services + Support Campus Safety and Security Student Health Support Services MyColumbia Portal Information Technology Student Handbook Student Success Student Financial Services Academic Advising Belonging and Persistence Holistic Support Career Outcomes Career Advising Alumni Success Rankings and Awards About About the College Facts Mission and History Rankings and Awards Academic Access and Excellence Strategic Plan Contact Us Leadership Office of the President Office of the Provost Board of Trustees News + Events Columbia Stories Media Mentions Event Spotlight 135th Anniversary Media Resources Careers + Alumni Career Center Internships Job Board Industry Partnerships Alumni Success The Alumni Network Get Info Apply Visit Give Search colum.edu Quick Links MyColumbia Canvas Library Academic Calendar Commencement Campus Map Building Hours Resources For Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Student Counselors and Advocates Faculty and Staff Alumni Donors Employers Health + Safety Campus Safety and Security Health Services Center for Student Wellbeing Services for Students with Disabilities Report a Concern Get Connected Give to Columbia Work at Columbia Hire from Columbia Directory Contact Us Get Info Apply Visit Give Search and quick links Open navigation menu Student Overview Student Overview Career Advising Internships Online Job Board On-Campus Employment Career Resources Career Advising Career Center Students Student Overview Career Advising Internships Online Job Board On-Campus Employment Career Resources Employers Employer Overview Hire from Columbia Fairs & Industry Events Host an Intern for Credit Partner With Us Employer Conduct Alumni Parents & Families Events and Programs Meet the Staff Location Student Center 754 S. Wabash, 3rd Floor 312-369-7280 careercenter@colum.edu Office Hours Monday–Friday 9am–5pm Walk-in Resume Reviews Monday–Friday 10am–4:30pm Make an appointment on ColumWorks It is never too early to start working with the Career Center. Students should visit us in the first year to explore career options, get their resume ready, and start thinking about part-time job or internship options. All alumni have access to career advising as well, but may have wait times during high-volume times of year as we prioritize students' appointments. Our team of experienced Career Advisors are available to meet in person or virtually to assist students and alumni with a range of career topics: Career exploration, planning, and goal-setting Resumes and cover letters Job and internship search Interview preparation Portfolio development Internship for Credit Program Networking On-campus student employment Using our online career platform Evaluating job offers Salary negotiation Preparing for career fairs or other on-campus recruiting Applying to grants, residencies, exhibitions or other art opportunities Graduate school search and application Freelancing and starting a business any other career or professional related questions Visit our Meet the Staff page to learn about our team members’ backgrounds and areas of expertise. All students are welcome to schedule with any advisor on staff. To schedule appointments: Log into ColumWorks using your Columbia single sign-on. *Alumni will need to complete the Alumni Request Form to request a ColumWorks account if you don't have one yet! Click “Appointments” in the left-side navigation. Select the type of appointment and the advisor you want -- check out the list at the top to see their specialties. You will be able to choose from in-person and virtual options. Walk-In Resume, Cover Letter, and LinkedIn profile reviews Writing your resume for the first time? Meet with a Peer Advisor first! Our Peer Advisors are trained by professional staff to provide resume, cover letter, and LinkedIn assistance on a walk-in basis. Walk-ins are only available to current students. Fall & Spring Hours: Monday–Friday 10:00 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. Summer Hours (May 19-Aug 29): Monday–Thursday 11:00am – 3:00pm If you have difficulty accessing ColumWorks or require assistance with scheduling, please reach out to the Career Center at 312-369-7280 or careercenter@colum.edu . Columbia College Chicago homepage Columbia College Chicago Instagram Columbia College Chicago Facebook Columbia College Chicago LinkedIn Columbia College Chicago YouTube Academics Admissions + Financial Aid Student Experience About Careers & Alumni INFO FOR Students Faculty and Staff Parents Alumni Contact Us Academics Schools Majors & Programs Academic Calendar Our Faculty Request Info Admissions + Financial Aid Application Requirements Portfolios and Auditions Financial Aid Scholarships Apply Student Experience Housing Campus Facilities Support Services Student Success Visit About News Events Rankings and Awards Mission and History Report a Concern Careers & Alumni Alumni Success Career Center Industry Opportunities The Alumni Network Give © 2026 Columbia College Chicago Directory Site Map Privacy Policy Accessibility Consumer Information Accreditation Suggest an Edit × ×"
    },
